00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.320
Point one: Do not buy expensive or luxury goods

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:40.800
The rational person, in the simplest possible definition, is the one who acts according to reason or logic,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.160
and therefore their behavior if making a financial decision will be in their financial interest

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:51.480
However, behavioral economists have discovered that a large proportion of the people do not act rationally

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.400
such as when they buy luxurious or expensive goods that they do not even need

00:02:55.400 --> 00:03:01.600
According to many sober and significant studies, a large proportion of consumers who buy luxurious goods

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.880
are in a financial situation that does not allow them to buy these goods at all

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:12.240
Instead of someone buying a smart phone at a fair price that does all the required tasks that they may need

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:18.160
We find that many people choose to pay a lot of money to buy luxurious phone brands

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:24.680
just to show off the brand they were able to afford, no matter that this pricier phone performs the same functions that the fair price phone does

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.520
Well, if your financial capabilities allow you to buy this expensive phone, that's okay, do whatever you want

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.280
but why does someone with a 3 or 5 thousand Egyptian pound salary, for example,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.520
afford to buy a phone or TV for 30 thousand pounds or more?

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.640
Behavioral economists say that this approach usually manifests a certain feeling of self satisfaction

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.640
wherein a person lacks self-confidence and does not respect themselves,

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.520
so when he/she buys these luxurious goods,

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:57.280
especially if they are financially unable, he/she enhances their self esteem, giving them more self confidence

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.800
The second reason is that a person’s purchase of luxurious goods,

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.440
though neither their income nor their financial capacity allows them to buy them easily,

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:08.680
is to generate a sense of belonging to an upper rich class,

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:14.000
this boosts a false sense of superiority to everyone around them, to be satisfied with their social class so to speak

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.120
However, sometimes this feeling turns against you

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.840
According to a study conducted by Boston College and Harvard Business School

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:32.080
spending your money on luxurious things is likely to lead to negative outcomes making you feel worse than before

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:39.040
This uncomfortable feeling that you feel after purchasing a luxurious good you can not financially afford and you don't need

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:52.000
is called the impostor syndrome from luxury consumption. Boston and Harvard researchers gave the study the same name

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:58.880
lest I bore you with this, you can never measure the value of yourself or success

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.925
by exaggerating the consumption of luxuries good in general,

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:04.560
otherwise, the result will be a shortcoming in things you actually need,

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:08.800
and an increase in the size of your debts reaching levels that you cannot repay afterwards,

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.480
thus wrecking your financial situation

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:19.400
To proceed with the second point, don't buy goods whose prices have been subjected to price shaking

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.240
Simply put, there are commodities which prices have risen dramatically in the recent few days

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:27.240
in a way that is not commensurate with their costs on the real ground

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.360
This happens as a result of an exaggerated reaction from the companies producing these commodities

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.520
motivated by greed and desire to make the best profit of the current  tense situation

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:40.200
However, when the situation gets better, these goods will come close to their fair price

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:45.920
Moving on to the second important point: Do not be carried away by installment offers

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:52.960
Can you imagine it when the same person whose salary is 5 thousand pounds goes to buy a phone for 30 thousand pounds in installments?

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:56.480
And this is often what happens because he simply does not have cash

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.680
Certainly, you have noticed the emergence of new companies in the Arab world

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:04.119
whose business model is all based on installment sales,

00:06:04.119 --> 00:06:07.640
whether this commodity is sold at interest or at the price of cash

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:13.440
These companies are the equivalent of “buy now, pay later” companies that exist in the West

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.320
In general, the business of installment companies flourishes much more in times of economic crisis

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:23.400
because people are tired of their financial conditions and they resort to buying in installments as a consequence

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:30.480
In a nutshell, I have two problems with buying in installments, and they are enough to keep you away from it completely

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.920
I hope you pay attention as this point is really important..

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:41.600
The first problem: that installment offers make you more susceptible to what behavioral economists call Impulsive buying,

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:42.612
which is a term that means making purchases of goods or services

00:06:42.612 --> 00:06:49.240
without planning for them and often without you needing them

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:54.080
In other words, you suddenly rush and buy something

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:58.720
because you were exposed to an outside stimulus, you are doing this without thinking

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.000
For example, you only have 10 thousand pounds,

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.600
so if you think about buying luxuries or something that is not necessary,

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:08.200
you may be able to buy a slightly expensive watch that you do not need

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:14.160
But if you decide to buy goods in installments, you can buy the expensive watch,

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.000
iPhone, PlayStation and sun glasses if possible. All you need

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.120
is to pay the first installment of each of these goods, and when it is the time to pay the rest of the installments,

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.360
you may be able to figure out how to manage them

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.960
The rest of these installments take us to the second problem,

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.440
which is the possibility of defaulting on paying the installments,

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:34.480
especially if you do not have certain assets that you can sell to pay the indebtedness

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:43.440
The installment is a debt that must be paid my dear, and if you do not pay in time , you will get into troubles, in addition to paying interest for delaying, you may be imprisoned as well, God forbid.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.680
One might say that this is a weak and unlikely possibility,

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:48.800
well, according to a study conducted by the American company Credit Karma

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:57.760
about 40% of users of “buy now, pay later” services failed to pay at least one of the installments

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.320
in America, this implicated them in late fines

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:11.760
Last Year, 2021 In Australia, the Afterpay company collected $64.6 million in late fines from installment service users

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:19.240
Of course, this will leave you in a terribly bad mood which may last for months or years until you pay off your debts or installments

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.240
Unfortunately the working environments in the Arab region are considered unstable

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:28.840
in other words, you may find yourself jobless at any time, with your income being cutted off, so how will you be able to pay your installments?

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.280
That's why I highly recommend buying in cash if possible

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:34.480
As the saying goes, If you can't afford something, think twice about whether you really need it or not

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.000
and don't forget the first point that we discussed before

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.160
The third point: raise your value to increase your income

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:48.720
Any good or service has a price, Your effort at work has a price which is the salary you receive at the end of each month

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:54.800
If you look around, you will find people doing the same job as you and getting paid more than you.. Why?

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.760
Perhaps because they are more experienced than you, this is one of the main reasons indeed,

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:03.960
therefore you have to raise your value for a salary hike. This isn't a HR talk

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:10.400
You should not waste your time even if you have finished your daily tasks,

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.600
as long as there is still spare time you have got to learn whatever skills you lack.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.240
If your salary is 5,000 pounds here in Egypt, ask yourself, what is the difference between you

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:22.760
and those who receive 10,000 and 15,000 pounds in the same field? Skills or experiences!

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:28.200
Well, sharpen your enthusiasm, get your skills augmented, gain experience

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.120
and last but not least make your goal to reach the same position.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:39.080
As I previously said, watch the time you spend as it tends to be what you are on now

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:43.120
The Fourth point: do not quit your job to follow your passion

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:50.480
Yes, I’d strongly advise anyone not to leave their stable job to follow their passion or enthusiasm especially in times of global economic crisis,

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:55.200
be wise, do not take risks in such times as this will probably cost too much.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:10:04.640
If your job ends at 4 or 5 PM then you have from 5 to 9, may be even 10 PM, as spare time, five hours per day in which you can follow your passion

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:09.200
whatever the way you wish, learn new skills, discover new fields - do whatever you want,

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.920
if you are a head of a family and busy with responsibilities making you have no spare time After work,

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:19.840
just keep your job, do not resign as long as you have no other guaranteed source of income

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.200
Only if you have a better job offer with more advantages do it

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:27.960
I highly recommend not quitting your job to launch a private business.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.000
On the other hand, establish a company or a project while you still are in your job,

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.240
no matter how hard to cope up with both, never leave your job

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:47.280
unless your project is really fruiting needing your full focus and there is a solid ground opportunity among other competitors in the market

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.400
The fifth point: Don't be reckless in launching business

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:55.920
Yes, I mean it, in times of economic crises and recession, do not launch a business recklessly

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:02.480
Of course, there are great opportunities in times of economic crises, but such difficult times are dangerous, and you are not a millionaire after all

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:04.960
You may lose the money you have and become financially broken,

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:08.840
so please do not waste your money on a project you barely studied

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:15.040
Do not invest in a field until you carefully study it in detail, consult domain experts,

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.120
and the greatest experience remains that you work in this field with your bare hands

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:26.320
Do you want to open a restaurant? Then work in a restaurant. Do you want to run a used-car business? work in a used-car showroom, and so on

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:37.720
Be careful! Don't rush out and pool your money in a mutual fund company, as these types of  financial vehicles are not trusty

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:42.400
You may think that things will work differently with you and you may be the exception,

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:50.480
I do not think so, my dear! Sure you can be the exception but this is less likely to happen, the more likely it is that you will lose your money and remain broke

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:54.240
Most people always think of themselves as the exception, and this is not wrong, by the way

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:59.800
Ambition is a positive attitude. The mistake is that you are really acting as an exception

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:05.480
According to National Business Capital, an American company specialized in financing and servicing small businesses;

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:09.820
90% of small projects or small companies fail

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:15.120
What is meant by small companies here are those that have 500 employees or less, do you get me?

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:19.800
90%! So, slow down, be wise, think twice about every step, and consult domain experts

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.080
Sixth point: Regarding gold

